# Ignored paths worktrunk copies into a new worktree.
#
# .beads/ is the load-bearing entry. The beads database is a per-project Dolt server, and
# bd resolves it by host and port from .beads/dolt-server.port. That file is gitignored, so
# a worktree receives it from nothing unless it is named here. Without it bd reports "no
# beads database found", and a run would mint a second empty database on its own port --
# measured: all four live worktrees of this repository held no .beads/ at all.
#
# Copying the port file makes a worktree reach the SAME server as the primary checkout,
# which is the property that lets an isolated worker's claims and closures reach the run.
.beads/
